# Everything that must not reach the image, loosely in order of how much it
# would cost if it did.

# Secrets. A COPY . . would otherwise bake the live API keys into a layer.
.env

# 1 GB, and rebuilt inside the image anyway.
.venv/

# Runtime state. SQLite caches and LangGraph threads belong to a running
# instance, not to an image - shipping them would serve one machine's cached
# answers to everyone.
data/cache/
data/checkpoints/

# Recording artefacts and the demo video: 240 MB of build/ plus 29 MB of mp4.
# The container DOES serve the video - views/about.py::recording() is the page
# for it - but it reads it from Cloud Storage via FINTOR_DEMO_VIDEO_URL rather
# than from a layer. Keeping it out is what makes that indirection worth having:
# the browser fetches the object directly and can seek it, and the image does
# not carry 29 MB that only one page reads. Without the env var set, the page
# falls back to the local file, which is how it works in a clone.
build/
docs/demo.mp4
docs/img/

# Source material for the brand assets. The generated .webp/.png files under
# src/web_app/assets/ are what the app reads.
*.png
*.pdf

.git/
# NOT .github/ wholesale. views/about.py::governance() reads
# .github/skills/*/SKILL.md and .github/copilot-instructions.md and renders
# them as the Governance page, so excluding the directory shipped a container
# that reported "Active skills 0" and an empty copilot-instructions tab while
# a local run showed five. Same trap as the 29 MB mp4 above: .dockerignore
# deciding an About page has nothing to show. Workflows are the part that is
# genuinely build-only, so that is the part excluded.
.github/workflows/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
tests/
scripts/
